{#
  Normalises a stored legacy URL into something linkable.

  Every legacy link on the site resolves through this one partial, so the host
  changes in one place when the legacy archive moves. The host comes from
  LEGACY_HOST in .env, exposed as craft.app.config.custom.legacyHost.

  The data holds several shapes, so prefixing every value with the host produced
  broken links: /scvhistory/lw3730.htm, scvhistory.com/scvhistory/lw3730.htm
  and, where a website landed in the legacy field by mistake,
  sangabrielmission.org. That last one rendered as
  https://scvhistory.comsangabrielmission.org.

  Rules: an absolute URL is used as is; a protocol-relative value gains https;
  a value starting with / is resolved against the legacy host; anything else is
  treated as its own host.

  sourcePath is provenance, keeps its full stored host and does not come here.

  Usage: {% set href = include('_partials/legacy-url', { value: legacy })|trim %}
#}
{%- set v = value|trim -%}
{%- set host = craft.app.config.custom.legacyHost|default('https://scvhistory.com')|trim('/') -%}
{%- if v starts with 'http://' or v starts with 'https://' -%}{{ v }}
{%- elseif v starts with '//' -%}https:{{ v }}
{%- elseif v starts with '/' -%}{{ host }}{{ v }}
{%- else -%}https://{{ v }}
{%- endif -%}
